  message: "INTERACTION NOTE from WI-kibah's branch (jgstern-agent/fix/kibah, 4 commits, not merged; the chained-call / method-on-result code was NOT edited there).\n\n1. The call arm's resolved emit now refuses a resolver hit outside the hinted package (_go_in_hinted_package, commit 3fb8b84d20). ListNameResolver falls back to the path-sorted first of ALL candidates when a hard path hint matches none of two or more, so a hinted chained call bound an unrelated repo method: prometheus `time.Now().Add(timeout)` -> test/testutils Collector.Add before, go:time:0-0:Add:unresolved on the branch. That is the hint this item's shape propagates from the inner operand; on the branch such calls stay unresolved under the inner package's slot instead of binding a wrong repo method. Expect a merge interaction in the found branch (`if lookup_result.found:` became `if lookup_result.symbol is not None and _go_in_hinted_package(...)`), and re-measure whatever this item counts after both land.\n2. The inner-operand import test of the chained-call arm (`node_text(inner_operand) in import_aliases`) is still position-blind: a local named like an import would hand its call the import's hint. The branch adds _GoLocalScope / _bound_names(site) (commit 92379e2067); the selector arm's own import test now asks `alias not in _bound_names(node)` (commit 0adbd3fa21) and the chained arm can ask the same.\n3. The call arm's construct for resolved emits is now stamped from the syntax (bare / package-qualified: function; value receiver: method) -- relevant if this item stamps a construct on method-on-result edges."  # c655
